  "mechanism_conclusions": [
    "D1 advantage appears in the first 28 adaptive selections and expands late rather than arising from one terminal lucky wave.",
    "Feasibility probability is informative (selected-set admission AUC about 0.706; productive AUC about 0.723).",
    "Uplift head is not strong globally (selected admitted Spearman about 0.214) but becomes strong late (about 0.604 in the final 28 adaptive asks).",
    "D2 feasibility-gated TPE preserves strong conditional economics but loses too much admission/selectivity versus full Surrogate acquisition; gating alone discards useful ranking information.",
    "TPE/D2 legal projection is not shown to be harmful in this run; projected subsets had higher realized yield than direct subsets, so projection reduction is not an evidence-backed optimization target.",
    "Observed template-specific winners are hypotheses only; template routing would be a post-hoc policy and requires a fresh prospective test."
  ],
